This folder contains SPECFEM3D_cartesian model_aniso.f90 files with different 
anisotropic models generated from the Brown2016 map. Linear interpolation (and 
extrapolation) is used to generate maps between (and outside) the closest 
isotropic map to the Brown2016 map and the Brown2016 map. 

TRIV --> Brown2016 map
ISO --> closest isotropic map to Brown2016 map

model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_100.f90  --> closest isotropic map to Brown2016 map
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_090.f90  --> map with t=0.90 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_080.f90  --> map with t=0.80 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_070.f90  --> map with t=0.70 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_060.f90  --> map with t=0.60 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_050.f90  --> map with t=0.50 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_040.f90  --> map with t=0.40 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_030.f90  --> map with t=0.30 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_020.f90  --> map with t=0.20 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_010.f90  --> map with t=0.10 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_000.f90  --> Brown2016 map
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_n010.f90 --> map with t=-0.10 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_n020.f90 --> map with t=-0.20 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_n030.f90 --> map with t=-0.30 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_n040.f90 --> map with t=-0.40 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_n050.f90 --> map with t=-0.50 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO
model_aniso_TRIV_ISO_n060.f90 --> map with t=-0.60 on the direct path between TRIV and ISO

To use one of these models in SPECFEM simulations -
1. Copy the file of interest into the SPECFEM source code folder
   src/generate_databases/ and rename the file as model_aniso.f90
2. In the Par_file set the flag ANISOTROPY = .true.
3. In the Mesh_Par_file while setting the material definition for the anisotropic
   material set the anisotropy flag to 2

These models were generated using the notebook -
https://github.com/uafgeotools/elasticmapper/blob/master/Scripts/Seismograms/models_for_specfem.ipynb

Note:

- The generated model parameter values were multiplied by a factor of 10^9 before
  being written into the model_aniso_*.f90 files to make them consistent with the
  Brown et al. 2016 paper.